            <h2>SubMersion: Interactive Art Exhibition</h2>

            <div id="submersionBoxes">
                <div id="submersionText">
                    <p><strong>Context:</strong> Implementation of immersive and interactive technologies for an underwater sculpture art exhibition featuring works by Jason DeCaires Taylor.</p>

                    <p>SubMersion presented an immersive exploration of a virtual underwater environment with real-time 3D modeling, interactive digital sculptures, and spatial audio. The exhibition used sensors and projection to create a responsive environment where visitors' actions subtly transformed the underwater scene.</p>

                    <p><strong>Role:</strong> Research and implementation of interaction patterns, immersive displays, and system integration. I focused on how participants' gestures and movement could produce meaningful and legible changes in the virtual environment while preserving the poetic character of the artwork.</p>

                    <p><strong>Technologies:</strong> Real-time 3D engines, interactive sensors, projection mapping, spatial audio and responsive UI elements adapted for different viewing distances.</p>

                    <p><strong>Outcome:</strong> A successful public installation that combined artistic content and interactive technology to increase engagement and empathy toward submerged cultural heritage.</p>
                </div>

